| Jira in the Work pages (#3260): `forge/issues`, `forge/issue`, `forge/plan` and the forge writes read and change Jira issues in the one model, with the jira connector's sign-in (`JIRA_URL`, `JIRA_EMAIL`, `JIRA_API_TOKEN` in the secrets) through `jiramcp.RealJira`, the server's own REST client. Issues only, of the projects a folder's `.agents/folder.json` names as `"jiraProjects": ["PROJ"]`, in one JQL search; a node is `jira:PROJ-12`; `state` is open or closed (the Done category) and `status` is the Jira status; the first fix version is the milestone; the description and comments are Jira's rendered HTML, made safe, as Markdown (html-to-markdown). An issue's page has Start Agent, a comment, labels (the site's) and a **status menu** of the transitions its workflow allows (`forge/close` with `transition`) in place of Close and Reopen; its Plan is the issues whose parent it is, blocked by their Blocks links. A session labelled `PROJ-12` in such a folder, and a pull request whose title or branch names the key, link to the issue | Mac, Remote, web (the Work pages) | walked on scratch | — | 2026-11-02, a scratch app with a fixture Jira Cloud site (`Web/test/walk/forge3260-jira.py`, `Web/test/walk/work3260.mjs`) on the web page in headless Chrome, the Mac window and the Remote in the walk simulator; `Go/internal/jiramcp/forge_test.go` and `Go/internal/agentsd/forgejira_test.go` | `Go/internal/jiramcp/forge.go`, `Go/internal/agentsd/forge.go`, `Go/internal/agentsd/forgewrite.go`, `Go/internal/agentsd/forgeplan.go` | not yet read on a real site: the test site's `KAN` issues are ready (KAN-6 to comment on and move), its API token waits for Alex's emailed code (#3411); comments are written as Jira wiki text (REST version 2), so Markdown beyond paragraphs, lists and links reads as typed; no setting in the app for `jiraProjects` yet; the Mac's status menu not pressed in a walk (its pop-up is out of the walk socket's reach) |
